   "stem": {
      "text": "Air is pumped into a balloon and leaks out of it. Let A(t) be the volume of air in the balloon, in liters, at time t minutes, for \\( t \\ge 0 \\). The rate of change of A is \\( R(t) = \\sin{\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{3} \\right)} + 4 \\) liters per minute. At time t = 0, there are 30 liters. Using a calculator, find \\( A(2) \\). Show the setup for the calculation, and give the value correct to three decimal places.",
